# Line endings are decided here, not by whatever each machine happens to be
# configured with. Without this file a Windows clone using Git's default
# core.autocrlf=true rewrites every file on checkout, and every tracked file
# then reports as modified -- 515 of them in this repository, which buries
# real work in noise and invites someone to commit the churn.
#
# Text is stored LF in the repository and checked out LF everywhere. Git's own
# detection decides what counts as text; the explicit rules below cover the
# cases where it would guess wrong or where a tool demands otherwise.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows batch interpreters read these byte by byte and mis-parse a lone LF,
# so these are the one thing that has to keep CRLF on disk.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Patches carry their own payload; re-ending them changes what they apply to.
*.patch -text

# Assets, keys, and fonts: never line-ending converted, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.otf binary
*.ttf binary
*.pem binary
